**Traction** bounds motor force. On **slip**, encoders follow wheel rotation rather than body travel.

Motor force is 3(drive−vground/0.8) N per wheel, bounded by tyre grip μmg/2=2.45 N. When slipping, wheel speed is found from the motor relation rather than body motion.

Encoders integrate it. Full starts slip until about 0.146 m/s, then approach 0.8 m/s with τ≈67 ms.

Host half-speed time 50 ms agrees with closed-form 47.7 ms within a 5 ms step.

